  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 15 representatives of NGOs participate in an intensive training program on the following subjects, but not limited to: environment protection and economic growth, climate change impacts and its relevance with the energy and other sectors, climate change and sustainable development, renewables and energy efficiency, women empowerment and climate change, etc; 
- 1,000 (200 women and young people) small agricultural producers increase their capacities in access to markets, income generating activities with sustainable and green aspects mainstreamed;
- 5 in-country study tours organized for the beneficiaries of the capacity development program willing to learn from their peers about green and environmental-friendly business and to find out more about energy-efficient technologies and sustainable practices.
- 10 smallholder farms and 20 households benefit from the implementation of renewable energy and energy-efficient technologies (biomass boilers in greenhouses, photovoltaic, among others).</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">-No data available regarding the number of NGOs with increased capacities in climate change and its relevance with energy and other sectors, climate resilient livelihoods, access to markets, income generating activities with sustainable and green aspects mainstreamed
-No data available regarding the rural inhabitants who received capacity building in conservation agriculture practices, climate change and its relevance with energy and other sectors, climate resilient livelihoods, access to markets, income generating activities with sustainable and green aspects mainstreamed, disaggregated by gender, age, family composition and type of event
-No data available regarding the number of NGO representatives participating at ToT events 
-No data available regarding the renewable energy and energy-efficient technologies practices implemented by the women agri-producers and the households with economic activities led by women.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
